                "reply_count": 4,
                "retweet_count": 1,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "Late last night, President Trump's Office of Management and Budget released a memo to pause all federal aid (grant, loan, and assistance programs) today at 5pm.\n\nThe only exception is for direct aid to individuals, which means Social Security and Medicare.\n\nAny other type of funding from a federal agency will likely be paused\u2014potentially including Medicaid, federal-aid highway programs, housing assistance for tenants, child nutrition programs, and grants for colleges and universities.\n\nThis likely violates impoundment law, which blocks the President from unilaterally withholding money without the consent of Congress.  \n\nStay tuned.",
                "text_lang": "en",
                "text_tagged_users": null,
                "text_tagged_users_ids": null,
                "text_tags": null,
                "timestamp": 1738082483,
                "view_count": 2053
